# The owner lane: a pull request touching any path below cannot merge without
# the operator's approving review (`protect-main` sets
# `require_code_owner_review`). Agents act as `brokdar-agent[bot]`
# (scripts/as-agent.sh), which is not a code owner, so no agent can clear this —
# not by approving, not by merging, not by being the author.
#
# What is here, and why: the paths where a plausible-looking change is a
# security or data incident, and the paths that define the gate itself — an
# agent PR must not be able to change what checks agent PRs.
#
# Every entry is a literal path, no globs, and `scripts/check-codeowners.sh`
# fails the commit if one stops matching a tracked file: a rename would
# otherwise drop its protection silently, with GitHub saying nothing.

# Auth and session: the single-user login, the session cookie, and where the
# guard is attached. `deps.py` only DEFINES `require_session`; which routers
# carry it is decided in `app/main.py` (the open router vs the guarded one), so
# moving a router across that line removes auth without touching an auth file.
/backend/app/api/session.py           @brokdar
/backend/app/api/deps.py              @brokdar
/backend/app/api/routes/auth.py       @brokdar
/backend/app/main.py                  @brokdar

# MCP authentication: bearer keys, scopes, the identity tools act as, and
# `mcp/main.py`, which attaches the key verifier to the server — dropping that
# argument leaves every tool open.
/backend/app/mcp/auth.py              @brokdar
/backend/app/mcp/identity.py          @brokdar
/backend/app/mcp/main.py              @brokdar

# Migrations run against the athlete's only database; a bad one is data loss.
/backend/app/persistence/alembic/     @brokdar

# What is exposed, and how it is deployed.
/caddy/                               @brokdar
/docker-compose.yml                   @brokdar
/.env.example                         @brokdar
/backend/Dockerfile                   @brokdar
/frontend/Dockerfile                  @brokdar

# The gate and the agents: CI, this file, hooks, toolchain pins, the agent
# definitions, workflows, rules and settings, and every repo-tooling script —
# the gate's own pieces (migration heuristic, api-sync, ci-status, the identity
# wrapper scripts/as-agent.sh, this file's checker) all live in scripts/.
/.github/                             @brokdar
/.claude/                             @brokdar
/.pre-commit-config.yaml              @brokdar
/justfile                             @brokdar
/mise.toml                            @brokdar
/mise.lock                            @brokdar
/backend/schemathesis.toml            @brokdar
/scripts/                             @brokdar

# DELIBERATELY NOT OWNED, and the hole it leaves: `backend/pyproject.toml`
# (the import-linter contracts, pytest options, ruff rules), `frontend/package.json`
# (the scripts the gate runs), the lint and test configs, `backend/app/core/config.py`
# (session cookie settings) and `backend/tests/`. An agent PR that edits one can
# weaken the check that judges agent PRs and merge without the operator. They are
# unowned because owning them sends every dependency bump and every new setting
# or test to the operator too; that trade is the operator's to make, not a default.
